<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>TokenUsage on Tech Insights: AI &amp; Cloud</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/tags/tokenusage/</link><description>Recent content in TokenUsage on Tech Insights: AI &amp; Cloud</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:04:08 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/tags/tokenusage/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Updated llm-echo Debug Plugin Simulates Token Usage for Tool Calls and System Prompts</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/updated-llm-echo-debug-plugin-simulates-token-usage-for-tool-calls-and-system-prompts/</link><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:04:08 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/updated-llm-echo-debug-plugin-simulates-token-usage-for-tool-calls-and-system-prompts/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="updated-llm-echo-debug-plugin-simulates-token-usage-for-tool-calls-and-system-prompts"&gt;Updated llm-echo Debug Plugin Simulates Token Usage for Tool Calls and System Prompts
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;A developer has enhanced the llm-echo debug plugin to simulate token usage tracking for additional components in LLM interactions. The update enables more accurate cost and performance testing during development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-overview"&gt;🔍 Overview
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The llm-echo plugin acts as a non-LLM &amp;ldquo;model&amp;rdquo; that repeats input prompts verbatim. It serves as a testing tool for validating prompt structures and token accounting without invoking actual language models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-key-details"&gt;⚙️ Key details
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Now tracks tokens for: &lt;strong&gt;tool calls&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;system prompts&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;reasoning steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides simulated input/output token counts in usage reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintains existing functionality for echoing prompts and context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-example-usage"&gt;🧩 Example usage
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;uvx --with llm-echo llm -m &lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;hi there&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; -o thinking &lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; --usage
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;First I consider the prompt, then I decide what to say.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;{
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &amp;#34;prompt&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;hi there&amp;#34;,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &amp;#34;system&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;&amp;#34;,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &amp;#34;attachments&amp;#34;: [],
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &amp;#34;stream&amp;#34;: true,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &amp;#34;previous&amp;#34;: []
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;Token usage: 2 input, 24 output
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="-why-it-matters"&gt;💡 Why it matters
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This update allows developers to debug token consumption across more interaction elements, improving cost estimation and prompt optimization before deploying to real models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#AIDevelopment #LLMTools #Debugging #TokenUsage&lt;/p&gt;
